Quick Recap
•	Smali is the human-readable representation of Android DEX bytecode.
•	It acts as the bridge between compiled Android applications and reverse engineering.
•	Android compiles Java and Kotlin into DEX, not JVM bytecode.
•	Smali accurately reflects the instructions executed by Android.
•	Decompiled Java is convenient, but Smali is often the more trustworthy view during security analysis.
•	Extracting an APK with APKTool reveals the smali/ directory, where compiled application logic can be inspected.
Final Thought
Java and Kotlin tell developers how to build an app. Smali tells security researchers how that app actually behaves.
Every vulnerability, every authentication check, every hidden feature, and every security decision eventually becomes Smali instructions.
Learn to read those instructions, and you'll stop seeing Android apps as black boxes. You'll see exactly how they work.
